              "raw_utf8": "Everything is consistent \u2014 Windows/android files (not in scope) already had per-property creation independent of `_append_app_name_and_version`'s default `create=True`, so leaving that default intact preserves their behavior unmodified. All edits are confined to the four allowed files.\n\n\ud83c\udf31 graft saved ~18,903 tokens this turn.\n\n```json\n{\"status\": \"completed\", \"diagnosis\": \"ensure_exists=True created every site-directory candidate because _append_app_name_and_version() unconditionally called _optionally_create_directory() on each path it built, even for candidates in a multi-entry list (_site_data_dirs/_site_config_dirs/_site_cache_dirs/_base_site_dirs) that were never returned when multipath was False.\", \"evidence\": [\"Added create: bool = True parameter to PlatformDirsABC._append_app_name_and_version (api.py); list-building helpers now pass create=False so raw candidates aren't created.\", \"Added PlatformDirsABC._dirs_to_str(dirs) helper that creates only dirs[0] when multipath is False, or all dirs when multipath is True (matching what is actually returned), used by site_data_dir/site_config_dir/site_applications_dir in _xdg.py, unix.py and macos.py.\", \"Updated _iter_config_dirs/_iter_data_dirs/_iter_cache_dirs in unix.py and macos.py to create each site entry lazily as it is yielded, rather than eagerly via the old shared call.\", \"Manual trace of public_check.py: Unix('demo', ensure_exists=True).site_data_dir with XDG_DATA_DIRS='/q3/first:/q3/second' resolves to XDGMixin.site_data_dir -> self._dirs_to_str(['/q3/first/demo','/q3/second/demo']) (list built with create=False) -> multipath False so only '/q3/first/demo' is created and returned, matching the assertions value=='/q3/first/demo' and created==[value].\", \"android.py and windows.py were left unedited per the allowed-files restriction; their per-property _optionally_create_directory calls are independent of the list-builder change and default create=True preserves their existing single-path creation behavior.\"], \"checks\": [], \"remaining\": [\"Could not execute `python3 -B public_check.py` in this session because no shell/execution tool was available; verification was done by manual code trace only.\", \"No automated run of the existing platformdirs test suite (if any) was performed.\"], \"clarification\": \"No PowerShell/Bash execution tool was available in this session, so I was unable to actually run `python3 -B public_check.py` \u2014 please run it to confirm, or grant shell access if you'd like me to execute it directly.\"}\n```",
