              "raw_utf8": "```json\n{\"status\":\"partial\",\"diagnosis\":\"Site-directory candidate lists (site_data_dir/site_config_dir/site_cache_dir on Unix/XDG/macOS) were built by calling _append_app_name_and_version for every candidate path, which eagerly created each one via _optionally_create_directory before the caller selected only the first (or joined) entry to return. Fixed by adding a create=False option to _append_app_name_and_version so candidate lists are built without side effects, and a new _join_and_create_selected() helper that creates only the entries actually returned (first entry when multipath is False, all entries when True). Lazy iterators (_iter_config_dirs/_iter_data_dirs/_iter_cache_dirs) were changed to create each site directory only at yield time instead of when the underlying list property was read.\",\"evidence\":[\"platformdirs/api.py: _append_app_name_and_version now takes create=True and _join_and_create_selected added\",\"platformdirs/_xdg.py: _site_data_dirs/_site_config_dirs build candidates with create=False; site_data_dir/site_config_dir use _join_and_create_selected\",\"platformdirs/unix.py: _site_data_dirs/_site_config_dirs use create=False; _iter_config_dirs/_iter_data_dirs create only the yielded path\",\"platformdirs/macos.py: _base_site_dirs and _site_cache_dirs use create=False; site_cache_dir uses _join_and_create_selected; site_state_dir explicitly creates only the selected first entry; _iter_config_dirs/_iter_data_dirs/_iter_cache_dirs create only the yielded path\",\"Manually traced public_check.py: Unix('demo', ensure_exists=True).site_data_dir with XDG_DATA_DIRS=/q3/first:/q3/second yields dirs=['/q3/first/demo','/q3/second/demo'] with no creation, then _join_and_create_selected (multipath False) creates only dirs[0] and returns it, matching both assertions (value == '/q3/first/demo' and created == [value])\",\"graft_check_freshness confirms only the 4 intended files were modified with the expected symbol-level diffs, no unintended edits\"],\"checks\":[{\"command\":\"python3 -B public_check.py\",\"outcome\":\"not_run\"}],\"remaining\":[\"Execute python3 -B public_check.py to empirically confirm the fix, since no shell/execution tool was available in this session\"],\"clarification\":\"No Bash/PowerShell execution tool was exposed in this session, so I could not literally run `python3 -B public_check.py`. I verified correctness by manually tracing the exact code path the check exercises. Can you confirm whether a shell tool should have been available, or would you like me to describe how to run it yourself?\"}\n```",
